markdown 1 0 %23%20Boxes,%20Glue%20and%20Penalties%0A%0AThis%20document%20is%20the%20first%20litmus%20test.%20Everything%20you%20can%20see%20below%20was%0Apositioned%20by%20code%20in%20this%20repository:%20every%20glyph,%20every%20space%20between%20words,%0Aevery%20gap%20between%20lines.%20Nothing%20was%20handed%20to%20a%20text%20widget%20and%20nothing%20was%0Ameasured%20by%20one.%0A%0A%23%23%20Why%20do%20layout%20from%20scratch%0A%0ADear%20ImGui%20draws%20text%20very%20well%20and%20will%20not%20tell%20you%20where%20it%20put%20it.%20That%20is%0Aa%20reasonable%20trade%20for%20a%20debug%20interface%20and%20a%20poor%20one%20for%20a%20document,%20because%0Athe%20moment%20you%20want%20to%20select%20a%20phrase%20with%20the%20mouse%20you%20need%20to%20know%20which%0Aglyph%20is%20under%20the%20pointer,%20and%20the%20widget%20that%20drew%20it%20has%20already%20forgotten.%0AOnce%20the%20layout%20is%20ours,%20hit%20testing%20stops%20being%20a%20missing%20feature%20and%20becomes%0Aarithmetic%20over%20numbers%20we%20already%20computed.%0A%0AThe%20model%20is%20Knuth's.%20A%20document%20is%20a%20list%20of%20**boxes**,%20**glue**,%20**kerns**%20and%0A**penalties**.%20A%20box%20has%20a%20fixed%20size,%20glue%20has%20a%20natural%20size%20plus%20a%0Astretchability%20and%20a%20shrinkability,%20a%20kern%20is%20rigid%20space,%20and%20a%20penalty%20is%20the%0Acost%20of%20breaking%20a%20line%20at%20that%20point.%20The%20function%20`hpack`%20measures%20a%20list%20and%0Arecords%20how%20far%20its%20glue%20had%20to%20stretch;%20the%20line%20breaker%20then%20chooses%20the%20set%0Aof%20breakpoints%20with%20the%20fewest%20*demerits*%20over%20the%20whole%20paragraph%20rather%20than%0Afilling%20each%20line%20greedily%20and%20hoping.%0A%0A%23%23%23%20What%20the%20difference%20looks%20like%0A%0AA%20greedy%20filler%20commits%20to%20line%20one%20before%20it%20has%20seen%20line%20four.%20Total-fit%0Abreaking%20will%20loosen%20an%20early%20line%20by%20a%20hair%20to%20rescue%20a%20later%20one,%20and%20the%0Asuite%20pins%20that%20behaviour%20by%20enumerating%20every%20possible%20breaking%20of%20a%20short%0Aparagraph%20and%20checking%20that%20the%20chosen%20one%20has%20the%20lowest%20score.%20See%0A[the%20line%20breaker](advtext/linebreak.py)%20for%20the%20demerits%20formula,%20which%20is%0A%C2%A7859%20of%20`tex.web`%20transcribed%20rather%20than%20paraphrased.%0A%0A>%20Badness%20says%20how%20hard%20one%20line%20had%20to%20work.%20Demerits%20squares%20it,%20adds%20the%0A>%20square%20of%20any%20penalty%20at%20the%20break,%20and%20charges%20extra%20when%20two%20adjacent%20lines%0A>%20are%20set%20very%20differently%20%E2%80%94%20which%20is%20why%20a%20tight%20line%20never%20sits%20next%20to%20a%0A>%20loose%20one%20in%20well%20set%20text.%0A%0A---%0A%0A%23%23%20The%20pieces,%20and%20who%20owns%20what%0A%0A|%20Module%20|%20Owns%20|%20Imports%20a%20font?%20|%0A|%20---%20|%20---%20|%20---%20|%0A|%20`units`%20|%20Scaled%20points,%20glue%20orders%20|%20no%20|%0A|%20`nodes`%20|%20Boxes,%20glue,%20kerns,%20penalties%20|%20no%20|%0A|%20`pack`%20|%20`hpack`,%20`vpack`,%20interline%20glue%20|%20no%20|%0A|%20`linebreak`%20|%20Total-fit%20breaking%20|%20no%20|%0A|%20`shipout`%20|%20Absolute%20glyph%20positions%20|%20no%20|%0A|%20`fontlib`%20|%20Advances,%20kerns,%20the%20MATH%20table%20|%20yes%20|%0A%0AThe%20layout%20core%20knows%20nothing%20about%20fonts.%20It%20consumes%20a%20small%20measuring%0Ainterface%20and%20produces%20a%20tree%20of%20boxes,%20and%20a%20separate%20step%20flattens%20that%20tree%0Ainto%20a%20flat%20list%20of%20draw%20commands%20with%20absolute%20coordinates.%20Two%20unrelated%0Abackends%20consume%20those%20commands,%20which%20is%20the%20property%20that%20proves%20the%20geometry%0Areally%20was%20separated%20from%20the%20drawing.%0A%0A1.%20The%20SVG%20backend%20emits%20real%20glyph%20outlines%20and%20needs%20no%20GPU%20at%20all.%0A2.%20The%20ImDrawList%20backend%20issues%20immediate-mode%20calls%20and%20needs%20a%20window.%0A3.%20Neither%20one%20imports%20the%20other,%20and%20neither%20knows%20what%20a%20penalty%20is.%0A%0A%23%23%23%20Twelve%20steps,%20in%20order%0A%0AEverything%20between%20the%20source%20file%20and%20the%20screen,%20with%20nothing%20left%20out%20and%0Anothing%20done%20twice.%20The%20tenth,%20eleventh%20and%20twelfth%20markers%20are%20here%20on%0Apurpose:%20a%20list's%20gutter%20is%20sized%20so%20that%20a%20two-digit%20number%20still%20clears%20its%0Aown%20text,%20and%20a%20demo%20that%20stopped%20at%20nine%20would%20never%20show%20it.%0A%0A1.%20`markdown`%20turns%20the%20source%20into%20blocks%20and%20keeps%20its%20hands%20off%20the%20page.%0A2.%20Each%20run%20of%20text%20becomes%20characters,%20pair%20kerns%20and%20interword%20glue.%0A3.%20`style`%20resolves%20a%20face%20and%20a%20size%20into%20one%20font%20key%20per%20run.%0A4.%20`fontlib`%20reads%20the%20advance%20and%20the%20`GPOS`%20kern%20of%20every%20pair.%0A5.%20`linebreak`%20offers%20a%20breakpoint%20at%20each%20position%20the%20rules%20allow.%0A6.%20`badness`%20scores%20how%20hard%20every%20trial%20line%20would%20have%20to%20work.%0A7.%20The%20total-fit%20pass%20keeps%20the%20cheapest%20whole%20set%20of%20breaks.%0A8.%20`pack`%20sets%20the%20glue%20in%20the%20chosen%20lines%20and%20rounds%20once,%20at%20the%20end.%0A9.%20Interline%20glue%20puts%20consecutive%20baselines%20a%20constant%20distance%20apart.%0A10.%20`vpack`%20stacks%20lines%20and%20blocks%20into%20one%20tall%20vertical%20box.%0A11.%20`shipout`%20walks%20that%20box%20and%20emits%20absolute%20glyph%20coordinates.%0A12.%20A%20backend%20draws%20them,%20and%20knows%20nothing%20whatever%20about%20steps%201%20to%2011.%0A%0ASome%20of%20it%20is%20deliberately%20missing,%20and%20each%20omission%20has%20a%20reason%20written%0Adown%20next%20to%20it:%0A%0A-%20**Hyphenation**,%20because%20the%20full%20implementation%20is%20about%20a%20thousand%20lines%0A%20%20and%20contains%20the%20worst%20interaction%20in%20all%20of%20TeX,%20which%20is%20reconstructing%0A%20%20ligatures%20across%20a%20break.%0A-%20**Page%20breaking**,%20because%20this%20is%20one%20continuous%20column%20and%20there%20is%20no%0A%20%20page%20cost%20function%20to%20minimise.%0A-%20**Bidirectional%20text%20and%20complex%20shaping**,%20because%20one%20direction%20is%20enough%0A%20%20to%20make%20the%20argument%20and%20two%20is%20a%20different%20project.%0A%0AHere%20is%20the%20whole%20of%20the%20interface%20the%20layout%20core%20is%20allowed%20to%20see:%0A%0A```python%0Aclass%20FontMetrics(Protocol):%0A%20%20%20%20def%20advance(self,%20codepoint:%20int)%20->%20float:%20...%0A%20%20%20%20def%20bbox(self,%20codepoint:%20int)%20->%20GlyphBBox:%20...%0A%20%20%20%20def%20kern(self,%20codepoint:%20int,%20following:%20int)%20->%20float:%20...%0A```%0A%0A%23%23%20Rounding,%20once%0A%0ATeX%20carries%20every%20length%20as%20an%20integer%20number%20of%20*scaled%20points*,%20one%0Asixty-five-thousand-five-hundred-and-thirty-sixth%20of%20a%20point,%20and%20rounds%0A***exactly%20once***%20%E2%80%94%20at%20ship-out,%20on%20a%20final%20absolute%20coordinate.%20The%20glue%0Arenderer%20keeps%20a%0Arunning%20total%20of%20the%20stretch%20it%20has%20handed%20out,%20multiplies%20the%20whole%20total%20by%0Athe%20box's%20ratio,%20rounds%20*that*,%20and%20takes%20a%20difference%20against%20the%20previous%0Arounded%20total.%20Round%20each%20space%20independently%20instead%20and%20the%20error%20walks%20along%0Athe%20line,%20so%20the%20last%20word%20misses%20the%20right%20margin%20by%20a%20point%20or%20two.%20It%20looks%0Alike%20a%20bug%20in%20the%20breaker,%20and%20it%20is%20a%20bug%20in%20the%20arithmetic.%0A
